  "independentDerivation": [
    "For an admissible C1 function, the endpoint relation gives f(0)=integral(fprime)/(k\u22121). Hence f(x)=integral[1/(k\u22121)+indicator(t\u2264x)]fprime(t)dt.",
    "Pointwise Cauchy-Schwarz followed by integration in x bounds integral f\u00b2 by [(k\u00b2+1)/(2(k\u22121)\u00b2)] integral fprime\u00b2. Therefore the best constant is at least2(k\u22121)\u00b2/(k\u00b2+1).",
    "The admissible affine trial f(x)=1+(k\u22121)x has derivative energy(k\u22121)\u00b2 and squared norm(k\u00b2+k+1)/3. Therefore the best constant is at most3(k\u22121)\u00b2/(k\u00b2+k+1).",
    "The two polynomial integrals are independently checked symbolically. Every literal displayed choice is decoded from explicit expression templates and enclosed using alternating arctangent series with rational remainder, plus a Machin pi enclosure. No float decides exclusion."
  ],
